==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|borborigmus}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|NL.}}, from {{der|en|grc|βορβορυγμός}}, of {{onomatopoeic|en|nocap=1}} origin.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/bɔːbəˈɹɪɡməs/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|borborygmi}}

# A [[rumbling]] sound made by the [[movement]] of [[gas]] in the [[intestines]].
#: {{synonyms|en|borborygm}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} Something resembling borborygmus.
#* '''1991''', Rebecca Goldstein, ''The Dark Sister'', Penguin Books, 1993, p.36:
#*: Finally, the emotional '''borborygmus''' subsiding, she produced, at last, the words: "It is said 'Bonnet.' As the hat which is tied beneath the chin."

